// anchor: json-namespace-value-scalar-target
// JSON is a compiler-owned class namespace, so JSON.value(x) is a method call
// whose receiver is a reserved builtin global rather than a value. Without an
// exact dispatch authority for that shape the native backend rejects the call
// as having no target, while the VM keeps running it: this case is the only
// coverage that pins the scalar encoder to one proven target on both paths.
fn main() {
    print(JSON.value(1))
    print(JSON.value(2.5))
    print(JSON.value(true))
    var encoded = JSON.value(-7)
    print(encoded)
}

main()
